C copyright status|Books at the Smithsonian Institution Libraries","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"Assessments":{"value":"","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"Artist":{"value":"<div class=\"fn value\">\nWatt, James, 1736-1819, author, correspondent</div>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"ImageDescription":{"value":"<div class=\"description\">\n<dl><dd>2 folded sheets (5 unnumbered pages)\u00a0: 30 cm or smaller</dd>\n<dd>Letter to Lysons containing recommendations on selecting and applying copal varnishes, with small hand drawn sketches of a brush and vial and an applicator consisting of \"a piece of fine sponge glued to a piece of wood.\"</dd>\n<dd>Title supplied by cataloger</dd>\n<dd>Autograph letter signed, handwritten in black ink on unlined paper with self-envelope and remnants of wax seal. Accompanied by a sheet of brown paper with an inscription handwritten in pencil</dd>\n<dd>James Watt FRS FRSE was a Scottish inventor, mechanical engineer, and chemist who improved on Thomas Newcomen's 1712 Newcomen steam engine with his Watt steam engine in 1776</dd></dl>\n<br>Subjects: Copal; Varnish and varnishing</div>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Credit":{"value":"<dl><dd><a href=\"//archive.org/details/jameswattletter00watt\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"iarchive:jameswattletter00watt\"><bdi class=\"description en\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\">Internet Archive identifier:</bdi> jameswattletter00watt</a></dd>\n<dd><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://archive.org/download/jameswattletter00watt/jameswattletter00watt.pdf\">https://archive.org/download/jameswattletter00watt/jameswattletter00watt.pdf</a></dd></dl>\n<ul><li>IA digitizing sponsor: Biodiversity Heritage Library</li></ul>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"UsageTerms":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page"},"AttributionRequired":{"value":"false","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Copyrighted":{"value":"False","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Restrictions":{"value":"","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"License":{"value":"pd","source":"commons-templates","hidden":""}},"mime":"application/pdf"}]},"122381395":{"pageid":122381395,"ns":6,"title":"File:Letter from Azim Jah, Regent of the Carnatic, to Queen Victoria.jpg","index":17,"imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"size":15816743,"width":3975,"height":7228,"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/60/Letter_from_Azim_Jah%2C_Regent_of_the_Carnatic%2C_to_Queen_Victoria.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Letter_from_Azim_Jah,_Regent_of_the_Carnatic,_to_Queen_Victoria.jpg","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:Redirect/page/122381395","extmetadata":{"DateTime":{"value":"2022-08-27 00:45:29","source":"mediawiki-metadata","hidden":""},"ObjectName":{"value":"Letter from Azim Jah, Regent of the Carnatic, to Queen Victoria","source":"mediawiki-metadata"},"CommonsMetadataExtension":{"value":1.2,"source":"extension","hidden":""},"Categories":{"value":"Nawabs of Arcot|1837 letters|PD-old-100-expired|PD-Art (PD-old-100-expired)|Template Unknown (author)|CC-PD-Mark|Victoria of the United Kingdom in 1837|PD-Art missing SDC copyright status|PD-old missing SDC copyright status|Victoria of the United Kingdom correspondence|Letters in Persian|Manuscripts in the Royal Collection of the United Kingdom","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"Assessments":{"value":"","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"ImageDescription":{"value":"This illuminated letter written in Persian dated 25 October 1837 was sent from Azim Jah, Regent of the Carnatic (1824\u201342), to the young Queen Victoria. He offers his condolences on learning of the death of William IV, \u2018on which event all the ceremonies of mourning observed among the Musulmans have been performed as a token of my sincere and unfeigned sorrow\u2019. The accompanying English translation made by an East India Company officer stationed at the palace of the Wallajah Nawabs, Chepauk Palace, continues with Azim Jah\u2019s hopes that \u2018Almighty God the Giver and Defender of the Kingdom of the Earth will make your accession happy and prosperous to Your Majesty as well as to Your Majesty\u2019s faithful adherents, whether present or absent; and that he will prolong Your Majesty\u2019s life, with the enjoyment of health and happiness, extending protection to all\u2019. The letter ends with the supplication, \u2018May the Star of Your Majesty\u2019s Prosperity shine for ever.\n<p>By the early nineteenth century, the region of the Carnatic was under complete British rule. As soon as Azim al-Daula (r. 1801\u201319) ascended the throne he was compelled to sign a treaty handing over the civil and municipal administration of the Carnatic to the East India Company. Its nominal rulers nevertheless retained diplomatic relations with the British monarchy, and this letter was followed by another dated 31 March 1842 to mark the birth of Queen Victoria\u2019s first-born son, Albert Edward. In this second letter, Azim Jah informed the Queen that he would be passing on his duties to his nephew, the Nawab, on his coming-of-age that August.\n</p>\nBoth letters are written on a narrow vertical panel set in the lower left of a much larger page surrounded by a wide gold margin and continue on smaller pieces of gold-flecked paper. Also surviving in the Royal Archives are the equally ornate English translations sent with the letters, one of the original gold-flecked envelopes and both embroidered bags in which the letters were sent, one with its wax seal still intact. These bags embroidered with metallic thread and iridescent beetle wing are extremely rare survivals of royal letter pouches.","source":"commons-desc-page"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"1837-10-25","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Credit":{"value":"<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.rct.uk/collection/themes/publications/eastern-encounters/letter-from-azim-jah-regent-of-the-carnatic-to\">https://www.rct.uk/collection/themes/publications/eastern-encounters/letter-from-azim-jah-regent-of-the-carnatic-to</a>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Artist":{"value":"Unknown author<span style=\"display: none;\">Unknown author</span>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"UsageTerms":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page"},"AttributionRequired":{"value":"false","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Copyrighted":{"value":"False","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Restrictions":{"value":"","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"License":{"value":"pd","source":"commons-templates","hidden":""}},"mime":"image/jpeg"}]},"198831160":{"pageid":198831160,"ns":6,"title":"File:Memoirs of Miles Byrne - Chef de bataillon in the service of France(,) officer of the Legion of honour, Knight of Saint-Louis, etc. (IA memoirsofmilesby02byrn 0).pdf","index":4,"imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"size":14667626,"width":743,"height":1281,"pagecount":260,"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/9e/Memoirs_of_Miles_Byrne_-_Chef_de_bataillon_in_the_service_of_France%28%2C%29_officer_of_the_Legion_of_honour%2C_Knight_of_Saint-Louis%2C_etc._%28IA_memoirsofmilesby02byrn_0%29.pdf?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Memoirs_of_Miles_Byrne_-_Chef_de_bataillon_in_the_service_of_France(,)_officer_of_the_Legion_of_honour,_Knight_of_Saint-Louis,_etc._(IA_memoirsofmilesby02byrn_0).pdf","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:Redirect/page/198831160","extmetadata":{"DateTime":{"value":"2026-09-04 06:41:49","source":"mediawiki-metadata","hidden"