pt at head. First front flyleaf includes two autographed presentation inscriptions, the first to Richard Trotter from his sister, dated 23 March, 1863, and the second to \"the hon. John C. Down\" from S\u00a9\u266damus o' Duileavy, dated 21 August 1949. Printed on wove papers. First rear flyleaf includes second-hand price in pencil script at head. Housed in protective archival envelope</dd>\n<dd>Boston Public Library (Rare Books Department) copy (volume 2) half-bound in marbled papers and sheepskin over pasteboard. Endpapers and edges marbled. Spine includes decorative rolled patterns in gilt, along with title in gilt over brown leather. Front pastedown includes armorial ex libris (bookplate) of \"Trotter of Mortonhall\". Printed on wove papers. Housed in protective archival envelope</dd>\n<dd>Boston Public Library (Rare Books Department) copy (volume 3) half-bound in marbled papers and sheepskin over pasteboard. Endpapers and edges marbled. Spine includes decorative rolled patterns in gilt, along with title in gilt over brown leather. Front pastedown includes armorial ex libris (bookplate) of \"Trotter of Mortonhall\". Printed on wove papers. Housed in protective archival envelope</dd></dl>\n<br>Subjects: Byrne, Miles, 1780-1862; United Irishmen; France. Arm\u00a9\u266de; Irish question; Nationalists; Revolutionaries; Exiles; Soldiers; Napoleonic Wars, 1800-1815</div>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Credit":{"value":"<dl><dd><a href=\"//archive.org/details/memoirsofmilesby02byrn_0\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"iarchive:memoirsofmilesby02byrn 0\"><bdi class=\"description en\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\">Internet Archive identifier:</bdi> memoirsofmilesby02byrn_0</a></dd>\n<dd><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://archive.org/download/memoirsofmilesby02byrn_0/memoirsofmilesby02byrn_0.pdf\">https://archive.org/download/memoirsofmilesby02byrn_0/memoirsofmilesby02byrn_0.pdf</a></dd></dl>\n<ul><li>IA contributor: Boston Public Library</li></ul>","source":"co